# Toolchain pin (execution-all-three-plan.md P0-02).
#
# Both apps declare `sdk: ^3.11.5` in pubspec.yaml, so the Flutter version must
# be one that bundles Dart >= 3.11.5. Flutter 3.44.7 is that version.
#
# It was NOT derived from the `flutter: ">=3.38.4"` line in pubspec.lock — that
# is a *minimum constraint* computed from the dependency graph, not the SDK
# that produced the lockfile. Pinning 3.38.4 on that reading failed CI
# immediately: it ships Dart 3.10.3, and `pub get` rejected it with
#
#   The current Dart SDK version is 3.10.3.
#   Because shipeast_customer requires SDK version ^3.11.5, version solving failed.
#   * Try using the Flutter SDK version: 3.44.7.
#
# 3.44.7 is pub's own resolution of the constraint, which is the authoritative
# source for this and the reason it is pinned here rather than guessed again.
#
# CI reads this file (.github/workflows/verify.yml and both APK workflows)
# rather than tracking `channel: stable`, so a Flutter release cannot silently
# change the build. When raising this pin, run `flutter pub get` in both apps
# and commit the resulting lockfile changes in the same commit.
flutter 3.44.7-stable
